@@section 2
@@title SQ-RP Spice of Life: Raspberry Pie Addition, 2026-11-12 ([raspberry_pie.md](../raspberry_pie.md) section 14, TODO `food/types-and-tuning #21`)
@@date 2026-11-12
@@jars creativebrewing creativedelight solraspberrypie
@@sources feature_writeup/raspberry_pie.md
@@text
@@text Targets `solRaspberryPie-1.0.0.jar` of 2026-11-12 20:47 (installed in `mods/`) with Apple Pie 2.2.0, the edited
@@text `defaultconfigs/solapplepie-server.toml` (benefits empty, `resetOnDeath = false`, drink blacklist) and
@@text `defaultconfigs/solraspberrypie/ladder.json`. Use a **fresh world** (both configs only reach new worlds). Rows marked
@@text "rebuild" also need Common + Creative Delight rebuilt (Diet Log name, Apple Pie potato recipe removed) or Creative
@@text Brewing rebuilt (Lava Walker burn); those two jars carry other unbuilt commits, so the owner rebuilds them. Most rows
@@text need a real player eating, so they are client rows (group `client`, a fresh superflat survival world, `/gamemode
@@text survival`; feed with `/give @s <food>`). Ladder thresholds below are the pack ladder's (slots at 2, 10, 30, 50, 75;
@@text flat Speed I at 20; 1 heart at 5, 15, ...); scale a check to what the world's diversity reaches.
@@text
@@table
## SQ-RPI-01 | boot: ladder loaded, no mixin errors, no Apple Pie warnings
@group A
@commands Boot. `grep -nE "solraspberrypie\|Raspberry Pie\|Mixin apply.*solraspberrypie\|InvalidInjectionException" logs/latest.log` (RPI-01)
@pass `Diet ladder: 38 rungs, 5 slots, 14 pool effects`; no mixin or injection error; no "Apple Pie still has its own benefits" warning; no "resetOnDeath is true" warning
@fails mixin target names in `development/solRaspberryPie/.../mixin/` (Apple Pie `initPages`, `m_7856_`, `updateFoodList`, `addFood`); world copied an old `serverconfig/solapplepie-server.toml` (fresh world needed)
@from batches/r1112/rp1.qb passed
bootexpect Diet ladder: 38 rungs, 5 slots, 14 pool effects
bootreject InvalidInjectionException|Mixin apply.*solraspberrypie.*failed|MixinApplyError
bootreject Apple Pie still has its own benefits
bootreject Apple Pie resetOnDeath is true
shell grep -nE "solraspberrypie|Raspberry Pie" logs/latest.log | cut -c1-300 | head -40

## SQ-RPI-02 | ladder.json seeded from defaultconfigs
@group A
@commands Same boot: `ls saves/<world>/serverconfig/solraspberrypie/ladder.json`; `diff` it with `defaultconfigs/solraspberrypie/ladder.json`
@pass file exists, identical (seeded from defaultconfigs)
@fails `LadderLoader.load` seeding path (`FMLPaths.GAMEDIR/defaultconfigs`)
@from batches/r1112/rp1.qb passed
bootexpect Seeded .*ladder\.json from .*defaultconfigs
shell ls -l rp/serverconfig/solraspberrypie/ladder.json && diff rp/serverconfig/solraspberrypie/ladder.json defaultconfigs/solraspberrypie/ladder.json && echo IDENTICAL

## SQ-RPI-03 | unregistered and unsafe entries skipped, ladder still 38 rungs
@group A
@commands Stop. In the world's `ladder.json` add `{"threshold": 3, "type": "unlock", "effect": "nosuchmod:thing"}` and `{"threshold": 4, "type": "flat", "effect": "minecraft:absorption"}`; boot (RPI-20, RPI-35, V10)
@pass exactly one line `skipped 1 entries naming effects or attributes that are not registered: unlock nosuchmod:thing at 3.0`; one `V10: flat minecraft:absorption` warning; still `Diet ladder: 38 rungs`
@fails `LadderLoader.parse` skipped / warnings lists
@from batches/r1112/rp2.qb
bootexpect skipped 1 entries naming effects or attributes that are not registered: unlock nosuchmod:thing at 3\.0
bootexpect V10: flat minecraft:absorption
bootexpect Diet ladder: 38 rungs
shell grep -cE "skipped [0-9]+ entries" logs/latest.log; grep -cE "V10: flat minecraft:absorption" logs/latest.log; true
look exactly one skipped line and one absorption V10 line (counts above both 1)

## SQ-RPI-04 | broken ladder file: loud error, built-in ladder, server runs
@group A
@commands Stop. Break the world's `ladder.json` (delete a comma); boot (V13, Q-H)
@pass `DIET LADDER FILE IS BROKEN OR MISSING` block; `Diet ladder` line absent but the server runs on the built-in ladder (`/solrp pause list` works)
@fails `LadderLoader.load` catch path; `default_ladder.json` in the jar
@from batches/r1112/rp3.qb passed
bootexpect DIET LADDER FILE IS BROKEN OR MISSING
bootreject Diet ladder: 38 rungs
> solrp pause list
expect rpb|paused

## SQ-RPI-05 | pause / resume commands
@group A
@commands Restore the ladder. Console: `/solrp pause list`, then with a bot or player `<name>`: `/solrp pause <name>`, `/solrp pause list`, `/solrp resume <name>`, `/solrp pause list` (RPI-37 commands)
@pass "No player has paused diet bonuses"; "Paused diet bonuses for 1 players"; list names the player; "Resumed ..."; list empty again. Stop and boot: list state survives
@fails `RpCommands`, `PauseRegistry` (world `data/solraspberrypie_paused.dat`)
@from batches/r1112/rp1.qb
> pbot spawn rpb 0 -60 0 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 3
> solrp pause list
> solrp pause rpb
> solrp pause list
> solrp resume rpb
> solrp pause list
> solrp pause rpb
> solrp pause list
expect No player has paused diet bonuses|solraspberrypie\.cmd\.none_paused
expect Paused diet bonuses for 1 players|solraspberrypie\.cmd\.paused
expect rpb
look none -> paused 1 -> list names rpb -> resumed -> empty -> paused again (left paused to check it survives the restart in rp2)

## SQ-RPI-06 | Raspberry Pie recipes loaded (CD half waits for a Creative Delight rebuild)
@group A
@commands `/kubejs` probe or JEI dump: recipes of type `solraspberrypie:diet_book` and `solraspberrypie:liquid_diet_log` loaded; `/zq recipes food_book` (`diet_log.js` loads from the pack's `kubejs/data/creativedelight/kubejs/`, no rebuild needed)
@pass both Raspberry Pie recipes load; Apple Pie's `solapplepie:food_book` recipe is removed (0 matches), no NCH remove error
@fails `data/solraspberrypie/recipes/`; `kubejs/data/creativedelight/kubejs/solapplepie/diet_log.js`
@from batches/r1112/rp1.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
> cdevtest bytype solraspberrypie:diet_book
waitlog \[cdevtest\] verb=bytype done= 30
> cdevtest recipes diet_log
waitlog \[cdevtest\] verb=recipes done= 30
> cdevtest recipes food_book
waitlog \[cdevtest\] verb=recipes done= 30
expect \[cdevtest\] verb=bytype serializer=solraspberrypie:diet_book n=[1-9]
# liquid_diet_log is a plain crafting_shapeless recipe (only diet_log uses the solraspberrypie:diet_book serializer)
expect \[cdevtest\] verb=bytype id=solraspberrypie:diet_log result=
expect \[cdevtest\] verb=recipes id=solraspberrypie:diet_log result=
expect \[cdevtest\] verb=recipes id=solraspberrypie:liquid_diet_log result=
reject \[cdevtest\] .*(done=0|error=)
shell grep -n "solapplepie:food_book" logs/kubejs/server.log | head; grep -cE "NCH.*(error|fail)" logs/kubejs/server.log; true
look record whether a `verb=recipes id=solapplepie:food_book` line is still present (expected until the CD rebuild; the recipes food_book call lists it)

